{
  "_about": "How to reopen each agent's conversation. exact/latest are argument lists appended to the flags the agent was started with ({id} = the session id); strip* are flags removed first so the new one is not doubled. `form: subcommand` means `<agent> [flags] resume <id>`. `probe` is what `kittymux sessions check` looks for in the installed CLI's own --help before it enables the agent here. verified:true = checked against that CLI's --help on the author's machine; verified:false = from public documentation, only enabled where the probe passes. Add or override agents in ~/.config/kittymux/resume.json (same shape). latest_scope: whether the agent's own help says its 'continue the latest session' is limited to the current directory (directory) or does not say (unstated: then it is only used when it is the single window of that agent).",
  "claude": {
    "verified": true,
    "locator": "claude-registry",
    "exact": [
      "--resume",
      "{id}"
    ],
    "latest": [
      "--continue"
    ],
    "strip_with_value": [
      "--resume",
      "-r",
      "--session-id"
    ],
    "strip": [
      "--continue",
      "-c"
    ],
    "probe": {
      "args": [
        "--help"
      ],
      "expect": [
        "--resume",
        "--continue"
      ]
    },
    "latest_scope": "directory"
  },
  "codex": {
